{"G1322":{"id":"G1322","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1322","disambiguated_id":"G1322 =","unique_id":"G1322","headword":"διδαχή","transliteration":"didachē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"teaching","definition_en":"διδαχή, -ῆς, ἡ\n (διδάσκω), [in LXX: Psa.60:1-12 title. (לָמַד pi.); Sm.: Deu.33:8 * ;] \n__1. objectively, teaching, doctrine, that which is taught: Mrk.1:27, Jhn.7:16, Act.17:19, Rom.6:7 16:17, 2Jn.10, Rev.2:24; with genitive poss., Mat.7:28 16:12 22:33, Mrk.1:22 11:18, Luk.4:32, Jhn.18:19, Act.5:28, Rev.2:14-15; ἡ δ., of Christ, Jhn.7:17, Act.13:12, 2Jn.9; of. τὴν δ., Tit.1:9; with genitive obj., βαπτισμῶν δ., Heb.6:2; pl., Heb.13:9. \n __2. Actively, teaching: Act.2:42, 2Ti.4:2; ἐν τ. δ., in the course of his teaching: Mrk.4:2 12:38; λαλεῖν ἐν δ., 1Co.14:6; ἔχειν δ., 1Co.14:26 (DCG, i, 485; Cremer, 181).†\n SYN.: διδασκαλία (AS)","source_line":1454}],"occurrence_count":30,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"doutrina","count":20},{"gloss":"ensino","count":4},{"gloss":"ensinamento","count":3},{"gloss":"ensinado","count":1},{"gloss":"doutrinas","count":1},{"gloss":"dourina","count":1}]},"G1355":{"id":"G1355","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1355","disambiguated_id":"G1355 =","unique_id":"G1355","headword":"διόπερ","transliteration":"dioper","lexical_morphology":"G:CONJ","gloss_en":"for","definition_en":"διό-περ conjunct. (διό, which see, strengthened by πέρ), \n [in LXX: Jdth.8:17; Jdt.8.1-36; 2Ma.5:1-27 * ;] \nfor which very reason: 1Co.8:13 10:14.†\n (AS)","source_line":1487}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"portanto","count":2}]},"G1588":{"id":"G1588","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1588","disambiguated_id":"G1588 =","unique_id":"G1588","headword":"ἐκλεκτός","transliteration":"eklektos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"select","definition_en":"ἐκ-λεκτός, -ή, -όν \n (ἐκλέγω), [in LXX for בָּחַר (so prob. in Isa.28:16, Pro.17:3, for MT בָּחַן), בָּרִיא, etc. ;] \n__1. choice, select (cl., rarely; Thuc., Plat., al.), hence, eminent: Rom.16:13 (cf. Eze.27:24). \n __2. As in Inscr. (MM, Exp., xii), chosen; esp. as in LXX, of Israel, elect, chosen of God (Isa.65:9, Psa.105:43, al.); so in NT; \n __(a) of Christ: Luk.23:35 (cf. Isa.42:1); figuratively, λίθος, 1Pe.2:4-6 (LXX); \n __(b) of holy angels: 1Ti.5:21; \n __(with) of Christians: Mat.24:22, 24, Mrk.13:20, 22 13:27, 2Ti.2:10, 1Pe.1:1; τ. θεοῦ, Luk.18:7, Rom.8:33, Col.3:12, Tit.1:1; τ. Χριστοῦ, Mat.24:31; ἐ. κυρία, II Jn 1; ἀδελφή, II Jn 13; γένος, 1Pe.2:9 (LXX); κλητοὶ καὶ ἐ. κ. πιστοί, Rev.17:14; opposite to κλητός (not so in Epp.; see Lft. on Col.3:12), Mat.20:16 (T, WH, txt., R, omit) Mat.22:14 (Cremer, 405, 775).†\n (AS)","source_line":1728}],"occurrence_count":23,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"escolhidos","count":14},{"gloss":"escolhida","count":3},{"gloss":"escolhido","count":2},{"gloss":"eleita","count":2},{"gloss":"Filho","count":1},{"gloss":"aos-forasteiros","count":1}]},"G1611":{"id":"G1611","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1611","disambiguated_id":"G1611 =","unique_id":"G1611","headword":"ἔκστασις","transliteration":"ekstasis","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"amazement","definition_en":"ἔκ-στασις, -εως, ἡ\n (ἐξίστημι) [in LXX: Gen.27:33, 1Ki.14:15, Eze.26:16, al. (חֲרָדָה); 2Ch.14:14 17:10 20:29 (פַּחַד), al. ;] \n__1. a displacement (Arist.). \n __2. An abnormal condition of the mind, in which the subject passes out of his usual self-control (Hippocr.); in NT (Kennedy, Sources, 121 f.); \n __(a) a trance: Act.10:10 11:5 22:17; \n __(b) amazement: Mrk.5:42 16:8, Luk.5:26, Act.3:19.†\n (AS)","source_line":1751}],"occurrence_count":7,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"êxtase","count":3},{"gloss":"ficaram","count":2},{"gloss":"espanto","count":2}]},"G1942":{"id":"G1942","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1942","disambiguated_id":"G1942 =","unique_id":"G1942","headword":"ἐπικάλυμμα","transliteration":"epikalumma","lexical_morphology