{"gloss":"prego","count":2},{"gloss":"divulgavam","count":1},{"gloss":"pregai","count":1},{"gloss":"pregas","count":1},{"gloss":"pregarão","count":1},{"gloss":"vontade","count":1},{"gloss":"proclamando","count":1}]},"G3022":{"id":"G3022","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3022","disambiguated_id":"G3022 =","unique_id":"G3022","headword":"λευκός","transliteration":"leukos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"white","definition_en":"λευκο-βύσσινος, -ον\n (cf. λευκολινής, a robe of white flax, C.I., 155, 17), \nwhite linen: Rev.19:14 (WH, mg.).†\n λευκός, ή, -όν \n [in LXX chiefly for לָבָן ;] \n__1. bright, brilliant: of clothing, Mat.17:2, Mrk.9:3 16:5, Luk.9:29, Act.1:10, Rev.3:5 4:4 6:11 7:9, 13 19:14 (cf. Ecc.9:8); ὡς χιών, Mat.28:3; ἐν λ.. (sc. ἱματίοις), Jhn.20:12, Rev.3:4; θρόνος, Rev.20:11. \n __2. white: Mat.5:36, Rev.1:14 2:17 4:4 6:2 14:14 19:11; figuratively, of garments, Rev.3:18; of ripened grain, Jhn.4:35.†\n (AS)","source_line":3224}],"occurrence_count":25,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"brancas","count":11},{"gloss":"branco","count":6},{"gloss":"branca","count":5},{"gloss":"brancos","count":3}]},"G3026":{"id":"G3026","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3026","disambiguated_id":"G3026 =","unique_id":"G3026","headword":"λῆρος","transliteration":"lēros","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"nonsense","definition_en":"λῆρος, -ου, ὁ \n [in LXX: 4Ma.5:10 * ;] \nsilly talk, nonsense: Luk.24:11.†\n (AS)","source_line":3228}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"delas","count":1}]},"G3073":{"id":"G3073","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3073","disambiguated_id":"G3073 =","unique_id":"G3073","headword":"Λυκία","transliteration":"Lukia","lexical_morphology":"N:N-F-L","gloss_en":"Lycia","definition_en":"Λυκία, -ας, ἡ \n Lydia, a region of Asia Minor; Act.27:5.†\n (AS)","source_line":3275}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Lícia","count":1}]},"G3143":{"id":"G3143","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3143","disambiguated_id":"G3143 =","unique_id":"G3143","headword":"μαρτύρομαι","transliteration":"marturomai","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to testify","definition_en":"μαρτύρομαι\n (μάρτυρ), [in LXX: Jdth.7:28, 1Ma.2:56 א)* ;] \nto summon as witness (M, Th., 25 f.; Hort., 1Pe., 53 f.; Lft., Notes, 29; Ga 203), hence, \n __(a) to protest, affirm solemnly: before ὅτι, Act.20:26, Gal.5:3; \n __(b) to adjure, beseech: with dative of person(s), Act.26:22; with accusative and inf., Eph.4:17; before εἰς, 1Th.2:12 (cf. δια-, προ-μαρτύρομαι).†\n (AS)","source_line":3353}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"dou-testemunho","count":3},{"gloss":"testemunho","count":1},{"gloss":"testifico","count":1}]},"G35":{"id":"G35","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0035","disambiguated_id":"G0035 =","unique_id":"G0035","headword":"ἀγενεαλόγητος","transliteration":"agenealogētos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"without genealogy","definition_en":"ἀγενεαλόγητος, -ον \n (γενεαλογέω), \nwithout genealogy, i.e. without recorded pedigree (cf. Neh.7:64): Heb.7:3 (Cremer, 152; MM, VGT, see word).†\n (AS)","source_line":128}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"genealogia","count":1}]},"G4051":{"id":"G4051","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4051","disambiguated_id":"G4051 =","unique_id":"G4051","headword":"περίσσευμα","transliteration":"perisseuma","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"overflow","definition_en":"περίσσευμα, -τος, τό\n (περισσεύω) [in LXX: Ecc.2:15 * ;] \nthat which is over and above, superfluity, abundance: opposite to ὑστέρημα (which see), 2Co.8:13-14; pl., Mrk.8:8; metaphorically, π. τ. καρδίας, Mat.12:34, Luk.6:45 (cf. Ec, l.with; Plut., al.).†\n (AS)","source_line":4173}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"abundância","count":4},{"gloss":"sobrou","count":1}]},"G4325":{"id":"G4325","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4325","disambiguated_id":"G4325 =","unique_id":"G4325","headword":"προσδαπανάω","transliteration":"prosdapanaō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to spend extra","definition_en":"προσδαπανάω, -ῶ \n to spend besides: with accusative, Luk.10:35.†\n SYN.: προσαναλίσκω (AS)","source_line":4455}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"gastares-a-mais","count":1}]},"G4435":{"id":"G4435","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4435","disambiguated_id":"G4435 =","unique_id":"G4435","headword":"πυγμή","transliteration":"pugmē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"fist","definition_en":"πυγμή, -ῆς, ἡ \n [in LXX: Exo.21:18, Isa.58:4 (אֶגְרֹף) * ;] \nthe fist: πυγμῇ νίψασθαι τ. χῖρας (Τ, πυκνά; Vg., Goth., Copt., crebro), to wash the hands with the fist (diligently, R, txt.; up to the elbow, R, mg.; the exact meaning is doubtful; see Swete, in l): Mrk.7:3.†\n (AS)","source_line":4568}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"lavarem","count":1}]},"G4921":{"id":"G4921","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4921","disambiguated_id":"G4921 =","unique_id":"G4921","headword":"συνίστημι, συνιστάω","transliteration":"sunistēmi, sunistaō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to commend","definition_en":"συν-ίστημι \n [in LXX for צָוָה pi., קָהַל ni., etc.; 1Ma.12:43, 2Ma.4:24, 3Ma.1:19 (and frequently in these books) ;] \n__1. trans., \n __(a) to commend, recommend: with accusative of person(s), 2Co.3:1 6:4 10:12 10:18; id. with dative, Rom.16:1 (as frequently at the beginning of a letter; Deiss., LAE, 226), 2Co.5:12; before πρός, 2Co.4:2; pass., before ὑπό, 2Co.12:11; \n __(b) to show, prove, establish: with accusative, Rom.3:5 5:8, 2Co.6:4; dupl. accusative, Gal.2:13; accusative and inf., 2Co.7:11 \n__2. Intrans., pf., συνέστηκα (as also 2 aor. and plpf.); \n __(a) to stand with or near: Luk.9:32; \n __(b) to be composed of, consist, cohere: Col.1:17 (see Lft., in l), 2Pe.3:5.†\n (AS)","source_line":5073}],"occurrence_count":